19-08-13T21:24:58Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nI have a scenario where I manually register a component (see example: https://codesandbox.io/s/react-hook-form-watch-after-empty-defocus-ukknu) but when my app moves to a different view, it tries to unregister and throws an error because the fieldsRef mapping is empty at that time.\r\n\r\n`removeEventListenerAndRef` is called from `unregister` with `undefined` as the `field` parameter. This method calls `findRemovedFieldAndRemoveListener` which tries to destructure the field parameter but it is undefined so it crashes.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nI tried to reproduce it in a contained scnario, but it seems to work just fine:\r\nhttps://codesandbox.io/s/react-hook-form-watch-after-empty-defocus-ukknu\r\n\r\nI don't know what is causing the crash in my application, but it's a more complicated stack with next.js and hot reloading, so probably something causes a delayed unregister or something like that.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nIf a field no longer exists in the fieldsRef, the unregister method should just ignore it (as it also ignores double registrations.\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nNot sure if this a long term issue and a good solution, but I think an extra null check would not be a bad thing?\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Nickman87","id":870416,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MDQxNg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/870416?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nickman87","html_url":"https://github.com/Nickman87","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nickman87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nickman87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nickman87/gists{/gist_id}","starr